Reading this as: redesign of an existing listening product for design-conscious
music listeners, with a premium-consumer / editorial-quiet language, leaning
toward Geist + York highlighter as the locked brand accent.

Dials: DESIGN_VARIANCE 6 / MOTION_INTENSITY 4 / VISUAL_DENSITY 4.

Before changing UI, read `.agents/skills/design-taste-frontend/SKILL.md` and
`.agents/skills/redesign-existing-projects/SKILL.md`. Then reference
`src/app/theme.css`, `src/app/variables.css`, and `src/app/tokens.json`.

Hard rules:
- Canvas is Bone White `#fafffa`. Headlines are Press Black `#121613`.
- Highlighter Green `#2bee4b` is the only saturated accent and the only filled CTA.
- Primary button: 5px radius, green fill, black 11px uppercase label, green-tinted shadow.
- Images: 14px radius and the green duotone filter. No full-color photography.
- UI type is Geist (York named TWK Lausanne). Display is the same Geist family
  at display size, never Inter, never Instrument Serif, never Fraunces.
- No em-dash or en-dash in visible copy. Use a period, comma, colon, or hyphen.
- Hero: max 2 headline lines, subtext max 20 words, CTA in the first viewport,
  no scroll cue, at most one small label in the whole hero.
- Maximum 1 eyebrow per 3 sections. Stack section heads. Do not split
  headline-left / explainer-right.
- Brand stays Resonant. No skip / next control.
- Homepage still names Listen Now, Favorite Songs, Connect Apple Music.
- Every Noise atlas is navigation only. Never write a genre field onto stored
  catalog records.
- Theme stays light (York canvas). Do not invert a mid-page section.
